          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A patient cannot abduct the left eye. Which cranial nerve is most likely affecte</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A patient cannot abduct the left eye. Which cranial nerve is most likely affected?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Oculomotor nerve (CN III)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>CN III supplies the medial, superior, and inferior rectus muscles plus the inferior oblique and levator palpebrae superioris — not the muscle responsible for abduction.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Trochlear nerve (CN IV)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>CN IV supplies only the superior oblique, which intorts and depresses the adducted eye. It does not control abduction.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Abducent nerve (CN VI)</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The lateral rectus is the sole abductor of the eye and is supplied exclusively by CN VI — hence the mnemonic LR6.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Ophthalmic nerve (CN V₁)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The ophthalmic division of the trigeminal nerve is purely sensory to the orbit. It carries no motor fibres to extraocular muscles.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Recall the mnemonic: LR6, SO4, all the rest CN III. The lateral rectus abducts the eye and is supplied by CN VI alone."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. The mnemonic LR6 (Lateral Rectus — CN VI) directly gives you this answer. Loss of abduction always points to an abducent nerve lesion."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
